# Normalise line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows, deployment runs in a Linux container. A shell
# script or Dockerfile that reaches the image with CRLF endings fails in a way
# that reads as nonsense — `#!/bin/sh\r` becomes "no such file or directory",
# naming a file that plainly exists. Pin them to LF so the checkout the container
# builds from is always correct, whatever the developer's platform.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
